      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nAlign the Torch sampler's top-p support with the ascending low-probability-tail cutoff used by NeMo-RL policy recomputation. For 16 equal logits and top_p=0.5, the old descending/shifted cutoff retained 9 tokens while training retained 8; sorting in opposite directions can also select different tied token IDs. A token sampled outside the recomputed support receives a -inf training logprob.\n\nRemove the ascending tail whose cumulative probability is <= 1-top_p, always keeping the highest-logit token. This intentionally changes Torch sampling at exact boundaries and ties, so old seeded outputs can change. It does not promise equal support for numerically different training/inference logits or change the FlashInfer backend.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nStandalone bug fix; no linked issue.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 13 new tests passed: CPU/GPU tied and untied cutoff cases plus a registered bit-exact GPU replay.\n- 4 existing Torch sampler tests passed on GB200.\n- Ran tools/autoformat.sh: Black, isort, pylint and Ruff passed. Its non-blocking mypy stage reports missing Torch stubs in the isolated lint environment.\n- No full model generation/convergence run on this standalone branch.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [x] Added a bit-exact replay and kernel manifest entry\n- [x] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [x] Documented the cutoff convention in code and compatibility impact above\n- [x] I have run tools/autoformat.sh\n\nDraft pending upstream review and CI.\n",
